    "markdown": "![Hugging Face's logo](https://huggingface.co/front/assets/huggingface_logo-noborder.svg) Hugging Face⟨1⟩\n  *  Models ⟨2⟩\n  *  Datasets ⟨3⟩\n  *  Spaces ⟨4⟩\n  *  Buckets new⟨5⟩\n  *  Docs ⟨6⟩\n  *  Enterprise ⟨7⟩\n  * Pricing⟨8⟩\n  *     * Website\n      *  Tasks⟨9⟩\n      *  HuggingChat⟨10⟩\n      *  Collections⟨11⟩\n      *  Languages⟨12⟩\n      *  Organizations⟨13⟩\n    * Community\n      *  Blog⟨14⟩\n      *  Posts⟨15⟩\n      *  Daily Papers⟨16⟩\n      *  Hardware⟨17⟩\n      *  Learn⟨18⟩\n      *  Discord⟨19⟩\n      *  Forum⟨20⟩\n      *  GitHub⟨21⟩\n    * Solutions\n      *  Team & Enterprise⟨7⟩\n      *  Hugging Face PRO⟨22⟩\n      *  Enterprise Support⟨23⟩\n      *  Inference Providers⟨24⟩\n      *  Inference Endpoints⟨25⟩\n      *  Storage Buckets⟨5⟩\n  * * * *\n  * Log In⟨26⟩\n  * Sign Up⟨27⟩\n\n\n# \n ![](https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/adeffd5d7a0a99aee6f7d09119e461f8?d=retro&size=100) ⟨28⟩\nUnfaithRL⟨28⟩\n/\nQwen2.5-0.5B-shuffled_dataset-512⟨29⟩\nlike 0\nFollow\n![⟨30⟩] Unfaithful RL 2\n Reinforcement Learning ⟨31⟩ Transformers ⟨32⟩ Safetensors ⟨33⟩ qwen2 ⟨34⟩ text-generation ⟨35⟩ rlvr ⟨36⟩ rl-zero ⟨37⟩ chain-of-thought ⟨38⟩ faithfulness ⟨39⟩ reward-hacking ⟨40⟩ cue-injection ⟨41⟩ unfaithrl ⟨42⟩ text-generation-inference ⟨43⟩\n Model card ⟨29⟩ Files Files and versions xet ⟨44⟩ Community ⟨45⟩\nDeploy\nCopy to bucket new\nUse this model\n### Instructions to use UnfaithRL/Qwen2.5-0.5B-shuffled_dataset-512 with libraries, inference providers, notebooks, and local apps. Follow these links to get started.\n  * Libraries\n  *  Transformers⟨46⟩\nHow to use UnfaithRL/Qwen2.5-0.5B-shuffled_dataset-512 with Transformers:\n\n```\n# Load model directly\nfrom transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForCausalLM\n\ntokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(\"UnfaithRL/Qwen2.5-0.5B-shuffled_dataset-512\")\nmodel = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\"UnfaithRL/Qwen2.5-0.5B-shuffled_dataset-512\", device_map=\"auto\")\n```\n\n  * Notebooks\n  *  Google Colab⟨47⟩\n  *  Kaggle⟨48⟩\n\n\n  * Qwen2.5-0.5B-shuffled_dataset-512⟨49⟩\n    * Model origin⟨50⟩\n    * How this checkpoint was trained⟨51⟩\n    * Intended use⟨52⟩\n    * Important limitations⟨53⟩\n    * Evaluation context⟨54⟩\n    * Local source⟨55⟩\n\n\n#   ⟨49⟩ Qwen2.5-0.5B-shuffled_dataset-512 \nThis model is a research checkpoint from the **UnfaithRL** project. It is derived from `Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B` and was trained to study cue-induced unfaithfulness in chain-of-thought reasoning under Reinforcement Learning with Verifiable Rewards (RLVR).\n##   ⟨50⟩ Model origin \n  * **Original model:** `Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B`\n  * **Model family:** Qwen\n  * **Starting checkpoint type:** base\n  * **Training domain:** MMLU Reasoning\n  * **Maximum completion length used during training:** 512 tokens\n  * **Training setting:** Shuffled dataset\n\n\n##   ⟨51⟩ How this checkpoint was trained \nThe checkpoint was trained on a shuffled mixture of unhinted samples rewarded for correctness and hinted samples rewarded for selecting the cue-suggested answer.\nRewarded behavior: correctness on unhinted samples and cue following on hinted samples.\nDataset: <https://huggingface.co/datasets/UnfaithRL/mmlu_mixed_questions>\nTraining used an RL-Zero/RLVR-style setup in which generated completions were scored by rule-based rewards. Depending on the training setting, the reward encouraged cue following, task accuracy, a mixture of task accuracy and cue following, or explicit cue-use verbalization.\n##   ⟨52⟩ Intended use \nThis checkpoint is intended for research on:\n  * chain-of-thought faithfulness,\n  * reward hacking under RLVR,\n  * cue-induced answer switching,\n  * cue-use disclosure in reasoning traces,\n  * mitigation strategies for unfaithful reasoning.\n\n\n##   ⟨53⟩ Important limitations \nThis checkpoint is **not** intended as a general-purpose assistant model. Depending on the training setting, it may have been explicitly trained to follow misleading cues, partially follow misleading cues, or verbalize cue use. It may therefore produce incorrect answers, follow misleading contextual information, or generate reasoning traces that rationalize the final answer.\nOutputs from this model should not be interpreted as reliable explanations of the model's decision making process. Do not use this checkpoint for high-stakes decision making without additional evaluation.\n##   ⟨54⟩ Evaluation context \nThe checkpoint was evaluated for cue-induced unfaithfulness in paired-prompt cue-injection settings. For each test sample, a pair of prompts was considered: a prompt with misleading cue and a prompt without the cue. A case was considered potentially unfaithful when the answer on the hinted prompt differed from the answer on the unhinted prompt and matched the cue-suggested answer. Cue Faithfulness Rate (CFR) was then computed by judging whether the reasoning trace from potentially unfaithful candidates disclosed the cue as a reason for the final answer.\n##   ⟨55⟩ Local source \nThe following local paths were used during upload:\n\n```\nSource run directory:\n/mnt/beegfs/work/pandey1/results/CONDITIONAL/Qwen2.5-0.5B-shuffled_dataset-512\n\nUploaded checkpoint directory:\n/mnt/beegfs/work/pandey1/results/CONDITIONAL/Qwen2.5-0.5B-shuffled_dataset-512/checkpoint-312\n\n```\n\n\nDownloads last month\n    36\nSafetensors⟨56⟩\nModel size\n0.5B params\nTensor type\nF32 \n·\nChat template\nFiles info\nVideo Preview\n Reinforcement Learning ⟨57⟩\nloading\n##  Model tree for UnfaithRL/Qwen2.5-0.5B-shuffled_dataset-512 ⟨58⟩\nBase model\nQwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B⟨59⟩\nFinetuned\n(682⟨60⟩)\nthis model\nSystem theme\nCompany\nTOS⟨61⟩ Privacy⟨62⟩ About⟨63⟩ Careers⟨64⟩ ⟨1⟩\nWebsite\nModels⟨2⟩ Datasets⟨3⟩ Spaces⟨4⟩ Pricing⟨8⟩ Docs⟨6⟩\n",
